   <text:h text:style-name="P186" text:outline-level="2"><text:bookmark text:name="_Verse_by_Verse"/><text:bookmark-start text:name="_Toc233660284"/>Verse by Verse / Interlinear Pane Styles<text:bookmark-end text:name="_Toc233660284"/></text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"><text:soft-page-break/>These are used for formatting the verse by verse pane under <text:span text:style-name="T46">Books</text:span> <text:span text:style-name="T64"></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T46"> Layouts</text:span>. Verse by verse breaks the text into individual verses with up to two other translations displayed per verse in an interlinear format. Translation (or language) 1 is the current main language for the book collection. Translation (or language) 2 is the first extra language to be displayed. Translation (or language) 3 is the second extra language. Note the difference in numbering, therefore, in the style names.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P88" loext:marker-style-name="T54"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="Standard"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr2" draw:name="Frame36" text:anchor-type="paragraph" svg:x="-0.0035in" svg:y="0.0992in" svg:width="5.978in" draw:z-index="206" loext:may-break-between-pages="true">
